1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,071
ChatGPT doesn't know what it's

2
00:00:02,071 --> 00:00:03,182
going to say.

3
00:00:03,232 --> 00:00:04,002
It guesses.

4
00:00:04,002 --> 00:00:05,350
One word at a time.

5
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,220
Well, not even words.

6
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:07,548
Tokens.

7
00:00:07,598 --> 00:00:09,888
Your message is chopped into tokens,

8
00:00:09,888 --> 00:00:12,350
about three quarters of a word each.

9
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,836
Then it scores every token it knows,

10
00:00:14,836 --> 00:00:17,350
and asks one question: what comes next?

11
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:19,298
The cat sat on the… mat?

12
00:00:19,298 --> 00:00:21,313
60%. Floor? 10%. Moon?

13
00:00:21,313 --> 00:00:22,350
Almost zero.

14
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,493
It picks one, adds it to the sentence,

15
00:00:24,493 --> 00:00:25,662
and does it all again.

16
00:00:25,712 --> 00:00:27,352
For every single token.

17
00:00:27,352 --> 00:00:29,728
Hundreds of times per answer.

18
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,150
Here's the part nobody tells you.

19
00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:34,350
It doesn't always pick the top one.

20
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,337
A setting called temperature adds a

21
00:00:36,337 --> 00:00:37,520
little randomness,

22
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:39,850
so it doesn't sound like a robot.

23
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,792
That's why the same question can get a

24
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:44,179
different answer every time.

25
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,620
Comment TOKEN,

26
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:48,278
and I'll send you a free tool that shows

27
00:00:48,278 --> 00:00:50,625
how ChatGPT splits your words.
